WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.460
[DIALING]

00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:03.224
[PHONE RINGING]

00:00:03.224 --> 00:00:04.640
MARK MIRCHANDANI:
(DISTORTED) This

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:06.330
is an intelligent
automated system.

00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:07.650
How can I help you today?

00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:10.150
IVAN RAMIREZ: I'd just like to
check the status of my order.

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:10.326
MARK MIRCHANDANI:
(DISTORTED) Did

00:00:10.326 --> 00:00:12.030
you say you wanted
to place an order?

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:12.180
IVAN RAMIREZ: No.

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:12.335
No.

00:00:12.335 --> 00:00:12.490
No.

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:12.610
No.

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:14.540
I just want to check
the status of my order.

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:14.930
MARK MIRCHANDANI:
(DISTORTED) OK.

00:00:14.930 --> 00:00:16.120
I'll place your order.

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:17.030
How many units would you like?

00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:17.470
IVAN RAMIREZ: No.

00:00:17.470 --> 00:00:17.980
Cancel.

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:19.640
I want to check the
status of my order.

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:20.180
MARK MIRCHANDANI:
(DISTORTED) OK.

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:21.022
1,000 units.

00:00:21.022 --> 00:00:22.610
I'll place that order for you.

00:00:22.610 --> 00:00:23.318
IVAN RAMIREZ: No.

00:00:23.318 --> 00:00:23.817
Stop.

00:00:23.817 --> 00:00:26.190
Ah!

00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:26.690
All right.

00:00:26.690 --> 00:00:27.482
Welcome to "Take5."

00:00:27.482 --> 00:00:29.815
Don't you wish that building
intelligent useful chatbots

00:00:29.815 --> 00:00:30.490
was easier?

00:00:30.490 --> 00:00:31.670
MARK MIRCHANDANI: (DISTORTED)
Sounds to me like--

00:00:31.670 --> 00:00:33.910
it sounds to me like you want
to talk more about Dialogflow.

00:00:33.910 --> 00:00:34.390
IVAN RAMIREZ: That's right.

00:00:34.390 --> 00:00:35.620
MARK MIRCHANDANI: Do you
have a demo to show us?

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:36.411
IVAN RAMIREZ: Yeah.

00:00:36.411 --> 00:00:38.447
Let's go ahead
and jump right in.

00:00:38.447 --> 00:00:40.792
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:46.130
Here we have the
Dialogflow console.

00:00:46.130 --> 00:00:48.570
So let's go ahead and
create a new agent.

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:51.600
We'll go ahead and
call it Take5Demo.

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:53.900
We will select the
language, English, for now.

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:55.350
But you see we
have many options.

00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:57.230
And we'll also
select the time zone.

00:00:57.230 --> 00:01:00.690
Finally, we'll attach
this to a GCP project,

00:01:00.690 --> 00:01:03.330
and we'll just hit
create a new one for now.

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:05.870
Now that our agent has been
created, let's go ahead

00:01:05.870 --> 00:01:06.950
and define some intents.

00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:09.890
But before we do, let's look
at some of our pre-made intents

00:01:09.890 --> 00:01:12.740
that were created
automatically with our agent.

00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:14.960
We have, first, our
fallback intent, and also

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:16.310
our welcome intent.

00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:19.090
Let's dive a little deeper
into our fallback content.

00:01:19.090 --> 00:01:21.680
This intent will catch anything
the bot does not understand

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:23.360
and respond accordingly.

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:25.550
Here there's no need to
add any training data.

00:01:25.550 --> 00:01:28.210
But we can edit how the bot
will respond to our users.

00:01:28.210 --> 00:01:31.080
And by default we have some
examples here on the screen.

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:33.080
Essentially, can you
repeat that again, or, hey,

00:01:33.080 --> 00:01:34.580
I didn't catch that.

00:01:34.580 --> 00:01:36.860
Let's go ahead and go
back to the main screen

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:41.240
and look at our
default welcome intent.

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:43.040
Here the bot is looking
for users' input,

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:45.872
such as hi, hello, hey there,
or any other type of greeting,

00:01:45.872 --> 00:01:48.080
and will automatically
respond with its own greeting,

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:49.255
as you can see here.

00:01:49.255 --> 00:01:51.380
To make things a little
interesting, let's go ahead

00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:53.450
and edit the text
of the response,

00:01:53.450 --> 00:01:56.450
and have the chatbot actually
ask for the user's name

00:01:56.450 --> 00:01:57.920
as part of that greeting.

00:01:57.920 --> 00:02:02.540
So here we'll go
ahead and add, what's

00:02:02.540 --> 00:02:04.370
your name to every
single option.

00:02:15.747 --> 00:02:17.330
Now, let's add some
common ingredients

00:02:17.330 --> 00:02:20.640
that the user may enter,
such as hi, hello,

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:22.580
and a couple of other
examples as well.

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:24.590
This way the chatbot
knows exactly what

00:02:24.590 --> 00:02:29.019
to expect before it
gives us its phrases.

00:02:29.019 --> 00:02:30.560
Now, the great thing
about Dialogflow

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:33.380
is that you just need to
give it a few examples,

00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:36.960
and then Dialogflow will go
ahead and extrapolate for you.

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:38.760
We recommend at least
using 10 examples,

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:41.093
so that Dialogflow can get
an idea of the kind of things

00:02:41.093 --> 00:02:43.655
that you should expect
before it gives its phrases.

00:02:46.427 --> 00:02:48.760
And once we've done this,
we'll go ahead and click Save.

00:02:53.390 --> 00:02:56.780
Now, from an intent, we can
also add a follow up intent.

00:02:56.780 --> 00:02:58.916
As you can see, we have a
bunch of default options

00:02:58.916 --> 00:02:59.540
you could pick.

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:00.998
But for this example
we'll go ahead

00:03:00.998 --> 00:03:02.829
and pick the custom option.

00:03:02.829 --> 00:03:04.370
And now that we've
selected it, let's

00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:07.316
go ahead and dive into it.

00:03:07.316 --> 00:03:09.440
The first thing we're going
to do is edit the name.

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:14.030
And the name of this intent,
we'll just call it, saying hi.

00:03:14.030 --> 00:03:15.560
Now, just like we
did before, we'll

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:17.870
go ahead and add some
training phrases.

00:03:17.870 --> 00:03:20.204
Since at this point the
bot just asked us our name,

00:03:20.204 --> 00:03:21.620
we'll go ahead and
give Dialogflow

00:03:21.620 --> 00:03:23.210
different examples
of different ways

00:03:23.210 --> 00:03:25.490
that someone may say their name.

00:03:25.490 --> 00:03:28.760
As an example here, I'll
put just the first name.

00:03:32.600 --> 00:03:34.430
And you'll see that
as I add examples,

00:03:34.430 --> 00:03:37.280
Dialogflow will
automatically identify that I

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:39.470
put a first name, a last name.

00:03:39.470 --> 00:03:42.230
And even when I add other
words, such as my name is,

00:03:42.230 --> 00:03:45.770
or they call me, or
I go by, Dialogflow

00:03:45.770 --> 00:03:48.680
will still be able to identify
which part of the sentence

00:03:48.680 --> 00:03:49.650
is the name.

00:03:49.650 --> 00:03:52.650
And we do this by using our
natural language processing.

00:03:55.450 --> 00:03:58.700
If at any point Dialogflow does
not catch any particular name,

00:03:58.700 --> 00:04:00.970
you can simply select
that word, and then

00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:03.487
tell Dialogflow that that
is a name, that way you're

00:04:03.487 --> 00:04:05.320
making sure that
Dialogflow is understanding

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:10.512
the context of the input that
the user is actually giving.

00:04:10.512 --> 00:04:11.970
Now, as we scroll
to the bottom, we

00:04:11.970 --> 00:04:15.960
can actually add the responses
that the bot will give.

00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:18.630
And we'll have our bot
say hello, and thank you

00:04:18.630 --> 00:04:19.920
for chatting with me.

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:22.680
But since we want this to be a
little bit more personalized,

00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:25.370
we're actually going to
include the first name

00:04:25.370 --> 00:04:28.150
input of the user that was
originally given to us.

00:04:28.150 --> 00:04:31.530
And we do this simply by adding
a dollar sign, and then saying,

00:04:31.530 --> 00:04:32.520
given name.

00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:34.520
This will make sure that
whatever the given name

00:04:34.520 --> 00:04:37.950
input was we're using for
our output from the chatbot.

00:04:37.950 --> 00:04:40.924
And then we'll go
ahead and click Save.

00:04:40.924 --> 00:04:42.840
So now that we've built
a pretty simple robot,

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:45.090
let's go ahead and
look at a quick demo.

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:47.799
We'll go ahead and go to
the integration section

00:04:47.799 --> 00:04:49.590
where you see we can
integrate with a bunch

00:04:49.590 --> 00:04:50.860
of different partners.

00:04:50.860 --> 00:04:53.220
And we'll go ahead
and click on Web Demo.

00:04:53.220 --> 00:04:55.650
And here we have
our chatbot live.

00:04:55.650 --> 00:04:59.110
So we'll go ahead and say
hi to it really quickly.

00:04:59.110 --> 00:05:01.230
And we're prompted
automatically to say our name.

00:05:01.230 --> 00:05:02.855
And then we'll give
it a brand new name

00:05:02.855 --> 00:05:04.260
that it's never seen before.

00:05:04.260 --> 00:05:07.270
So here I'll put Enrique
Iglesias as an example.

00:05:07.270 --> 00:05:09.380
And it automatically
captured my name,

00:05:09.380 --> 00:05:11.610
and I was able to
say hi back to it,

00:05:11.610 --> 00:05:13.937
even though it had never
seen that name before.

00:05:13.937 --> 00:05:16.020
I know this is a really
simple demo of Dialogflow,

00:05:16.020 --> 00:05:17.820
but just now imagine
the possibilities

00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:19.890
making a decision tree
with different intents,

00:05:19.890 --> 00:05:22.410
and different actions, prompting
uses for different inputs,

00:05:22.410 --> 00:05:24.220
and then tying in
a back end that

00:05:24.220 --> 00:05:26.220
can have actionable requests.

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:28.412
This is just the surface
of what Dialogflow can do.

00:05:28.412 --> 00:05:30.120
MARK MIRCHANDANI: So
if you want to build

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:32.386
a great chatbot (DISTORTED)
instead of one of these,

00:05:32.386 --> 00:05:33.490
you should be using Dialogflow.

00:05:33.490 --> 00:05:33.990
IVAN RAMIREZ: Yup.

00:05:33.990 --> 00:05:35.940
And in less than five minutes,
you can be up and running.

00:05:35.940 --> 00:05:36.170
MARK MIRCHANDANI:
(DISTORTED) Please

00:05:36.170 --> 00:05:37.980
like, comment, and subscribe.

00:05:37.980 --> 00:05:40.355
IVAN RAMIREZ: And if you're
working on any cool projects,

00:05:40.355 --> 00:05:41.970
please click on the link below.

00:05:41.970 --> 00:05:44.720
[MUSIC PLAYING]

